      "text": "To find the first digit of the base 8 representation of \\(473_{10}\\), we need to convert the decimal number \\(473\\) to its equivalent in base 8. We do this by repeatedly dividing the number by 8 and keeping track of the remainders.\n\n1. Divide \\(473\\) by \\(8\\):\n   \\[\n   473 \\div 8 = 59 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 5\n   \\]\n   So, the least significant digit (rightmost) is \\(5\\).\n\n2. Divide \\(59\\) by \\(8\\):\n   \\[\n   59 \\div 8 = 7 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 3\n   \\]\n   So, the next digit is \\(3\\).\n\n3. Divide \\(7\\) by \\(8\\):\n   \\[\n   7 \\div 8 = 0 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 7\n   \\]\n   So, the next digit is \\(7\\).\n\nSince the quotient is now \\(0\\), we stop the division process. Reading the remainders from bottom to top, the base 8 representation of \\(473_{10}\\) is \\(735_8\\).\n\nThe first digit of the base 8 representation is \\(7\\).\n\nThus, the first digit of the base 8 representation of \\(473_{10}\\) is \\(\\boxed{7}\\).",
