      "text": "To find the first digit of the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$, we need to convert $473_{10}$ to base $8$. This can be done by repeatedly dividing the number by $8$ and keeping track of the remainders.\n\nFirst, we divide $473$ by $8$:\n\\[ 473 \\div 8 = 59 \\text{ with a remainder of } 1 \\]\nSo, the least significant digit (rightmost digit) in base $8$ is $1$.\n\nNext, we divide the quotient $59$ by $8$:\n\\[ 59 \\div 8 = 7 \\text{ with a remainder of } 3 \\]\nSo, the next digit in base $8$ is $3$.\n\nFinally, we divide the quotient $7$ by $8$:\n\\[ 7 \\div 8 = 0 \\text{ with a remainder of } 7 \\]\nSo, the next digit in base $8$ is $7$.\n\nThus, the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$ is $731_8$. The first digit in this representation is $7$.\n\nTherefore, the first digit of the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$ is \\(\\boxed{7}\\).",
