      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the first digit of the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$, we need to determine $8^2$ (since $8^2 = 64$) first. If $473_{10}$ is greater than or equal to $64$, we will have the first digit in base 8 in the left position. Otherwise, we need to subtract $64$, leaving us with a value between $0$ and $63$, and the first digit of this new value will be the first digit of the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$.\n\nLet's solve this step-by-step:\n\n1. Find the largest power of $8$ that is less than or equal to $473$.\n2. Subtract this power of $8$ from $473$ to get a quotient.\n3. Determine the first digit of the quotient in base $8$.\n\nLet's implement this in Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Function to find the first digit of a number in a given base\r\ndef first_digit_in_base(n, base):\r\n    # Find the largest power of the base that is less than or equal to n\r\n    power = 0\r\n    while base ** power <= n:\r\n        power += 1\r\n    power -= 1\r\n\r\n    # Calculate the quotient when n is divided by the base raised to this power\r\n    quotient = n // (base ** power)\r\n\r\n    # Convert the quotient to its digit representation in the given base\r\n    return str(quotient)[0]\r\n\r\n# Given number in decimal\r\nn = 473\r\n# Base in which we are converting\r\nbase = 8\r\n\r\n# Find the first digit in base 8\r\nfirst_digit = first_digit_in_base(n, base)\r\nprint(first_digit)\n```\n```output\n7\n```\nThe first digit (from left to right) of the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$ is $\\boxed{7}$.",
